ectives, units, bounds and uncertainty.\n\u2502\n\u2502    mbse-diagramming\n\u2502\n\u2502      Create or review source-linked engineering architecture, workflow, sequence or state diagrams in Mermaid, Graphviz or an available UML/PlantUML tool skill; preserve semantics and report actual rendering checks.\n\u2502\n\u2502    mbse-discovery\n\u2502\n\u2502      Clarify system boundaries, stakeholder needs, requirements and vocabulary before authoring or reviewing an engineering model.\n\u2502\n\u2502    mbse-engineering-plots\n\u2502\n\u2502      Visualize engineering constraints, finite trade studies, sensitivity or verification data with explicit units, uncertainty and provenance; use reproducible plots rather than decorative charts.\n\u2502\n\u2502    mbse-excalidraw\n\u2502\n\u2502      Create or revise editable Excalidraw engineering sketches with stable artifact mapping, meaningful arrows and explicit proposal status; retain the scene and review its exports.\n\u2502\n\u2502    mbse-grill-me\n\u2502\n\u2502      Interview a user adaptively to clarify or stress-test an engineering goal, plan, requirement or modeling decision; start open-ended and narrow to grounded choices. Use when asked to grill the user or work through uncertainty interactively, rather than for an already precise edit or a factual lookup.\n\u2502\n\u2502    mbse-literature-research\n\u2502\n\u2502      Find and assess MBSE papers, methods and related repositories with verified bibliographic identity, version, applicability and evidence provenance.\n\u2502\n\u2502    mbse-model-tdd\n\u2502\n\u2502      Develop test-first checks for SysML v2 model changes, collect pinned engine and LSP evidence, and investigate differing or unavailable results.\n\u2502\n\u2502    mbse-oosem\n\u2502\n\u2502      Apply a bounded OOSEM-inspired workflow linking stakeholder scenarios, requirements, logical and allocated architectures, alternatives and verification; distinguish the historical method from newer work.\n\u2502\n\u2502    mbse-requirements\n\u2502\n\u2502      Develop or review measurable system requirements, derivation, allocation and traceability independently of a modeling language.\n\u2502\n\u2502    mbse-standards-research\n\u2502\n\u2502      Find and interpret versioned engineering standards and institutional guidance and distinguish normative requirements from examples and implementation behavior.\n\u2502\n\u2502    mbse-sysml-modeling\n\u2502\n\u2502      Author, explain or revise SysML v2 textual models with relevant KerML foundations, typed quantities and explicit engine portability limits.\n\u2502\n\u2502    mbse-traceability\n\u2502\n\u2502      Build requirements-to-evidence traces and assess change impact across needs, assumptions, architecture, model artifacts and verification results.\n\u2502\n\u2502    mbse-verification\n\u2502\n\u2502      Plan and assess verification and validation evidence for requirements or model changes, including test-first checks, independently of engines or modeling languages.\n\u2502\n\u2502    setup-mbse-skills\n\u2502\n\u2502      Configure project conventions for this MBSE skill collection when onboarding a team or changing its modeling, evidence or verification workflow.\n\n\u2502\n\u2514  Use --skill <name> to install specific skills\n\n"
